SM-T715 tablet: tiles that do what they say.

Airplane mode turns the modem off too: it has no rfkill device, so that goes through
NetworkManager, and shannond keeps the radio off across boots. The Hotspot tile is
back under "Add tiles", now that the modem can be its uplink, and it shows its
password. The call card has no Speaker toggle: the tablet has no earpiece, so the
toggle switched nothing and read "off" with the sound on the speaker. Against
omarchy-mobile 5f7ba48, packages/omamobile-shell, after 0001 to 0007.
The modem and rfkill states are read with LC_ALL=C: the session runs in French,
where rfkill says "bloqué", and upstream's tile never saw itself on.

